 "result_text": "`pyflakes` no longer crashes on `__all__, = (...)`. I ran it on the example from the issue and it exits cleanly. The existing suite passes (714 passed, 44 skipped), and I added no tests.\n\nThe fix is in `pyflakes/checker.py`, in the binding code near line 1294. It only builds an `ExportBinding` for `__all__` when the name's direct parent is an `Assign`, `AugAssign` or `AnnAssign`. With `__all__, = ...` the parent is a `Tuple`, so the name now gets a plain `Assignment` binding instead.\n\nI did not add a warning for this form, as the issue suggested (\"mark this as invalid\"). It is simply treated as an ordinary assignment, so `fizz` and `buzz` are not read as exported names. Say if you want an explicit message instead.",
